- Alternative (production change, not ours): widen the guard in DynamicCardBundleBuilder to accept a new explicit source directory. That's a production edit; the contract forbids workers touching production, but root owns integration decisions.
- The "enable AllowEditorSourceLoading" shortcut does NOT work while a ready bundle exists, because DynamicCardLibrary.LoadCatalog loads the bundle and skips the AssetDatabase path (`if (bundle == null)`). Even with no bundle, the guard is only in the builder, not the loader, so source loading would work with a catalog merge. But a present cache wins. Do not delete/rename the cache.

