## Delivered

| File | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `Integration/Runtime/LadyLakePremiumFraming.cs` | Exact framing math (public, shared by builder/validator/runtime) |
| `Integration/Runtime/LadyLakePremiumStage.cs` | Runtime scene stage → calls the **real** `DynamicCardView.Bind` |
| `Integration/Editor/LadyLakePremiumBuilder.cs` | `public static Build()` / `Open()` / `BuildAndOpen()` / `ValidateAndWrite()` |
| `Integration/Editor/LadyLakePremiumValidator.cs` | Static validation (`validation-report.json`) + explicit `unverifiedRuntime` |
| `Integration/Editor/LadyLakePremiumEditorBridge.cs` | Opt-in file bridge on `editor-request.txt` (no auto build/play) |
| `Integration/catalog-entry.json` | The `DynamicCardEntry` (`lady-lake-authored`, `c10000000`, FOV 35, distance −11.5, pivot `Pivot`, 12/12) |
| `Integration/editor-request.txt` | Comment-only placeholder (bridge ignores it) |
| `Integration/integration-report.md` | Full report incl. framing math and bundle analysis |

`Integration/Card.prefab` and `Integration/LadyLakePremium.unity` are generated by `Build()` because the model/environment prefabs are produced by the concurrent workers. `Build()` reflection-calls `LadyLakeModelBuilder.Build()` / `LadyLakeEnvironmentBuilder.Build()` and throws a named error if either (or its prefab) is absent — no placeholders.

## Key design points
- **Real production path**: stage instantiates the collection `ArtCard`, applies the original gold/neutral sprites, calls `DynamicCardPresentation.Configure`, then `DynamicCardView.Bind(CardImg, "c10000000", largePreview:true, wholeCard:CardBorder, presentationRoot:card.transform, portraitBorder:CardBorder, premium:true)`. No cloned player/camera/drag, no custom RT backend, no injected library entries.
- **Assembly**: `Card → Pivot → {FigureRig, Environment}` as nested prefab instances; `entry.pivot = "Pivot"`.
- **Framing**: `Pivot = (0.053175, −2.042541, 0)` = anchor `−2` compensation plus the small ArtRegion-centre correction so the 497×710 (world 7.10) painting fits the unchanged `ArtRegion` (region world height 7.1151). Verified against the shipped source convention (`56180101/Card.prefab` uses `Pivot (0,−2,0)`), documented in the report.
- **Opt-in bridge**: `build|open|play|stop|capture|validate|sample|status|refresh`, absolute paths, `editor-result.txt`/`editor-state.json`/`stage-sample.json`. It does nothing unless the request file holds a command. I issued no requests.

## Bundle precedence (documented, not acted on)
The editor cache `Library/DynamicCardsBundles/StandaloneWindows64/cards.bundle` **exists and is `.editor-ready`**, so `DynamicCardLibrary.LoadCatalog` never consults the AssetDatabase fallback (`if (bundle == null)`), and neither `c10000000` nor the new id is in `catalog.json` yet. Root must: merge `catalog-entry.json`, **relocate the prefab** to a path the bundle builder accepts (it rejects anything outside `Content/Latest` / `Content/Old/*`), rebuild packages, then re-enter Play. The cache was not moved or deleted.

## Compile feedback handled
Unity was live; its log showed `Assembly-CSharp` rebuilt cleanly with my runtime files, and only four `CS1061` errors in the validator (`string[]` + `.Add`) plus a stale `CS0103`. I switched `checks`/`failures` to `List<string>`; the report notes root should send `refresh` before `build` since the editor assembly hadn't recompiled again yet.
